      "en": "Brighton and Hove, located on the south coast of England in East Sussex, represents a unique blend of historic charm and modern, eccentric culture. The city was formed by the merging of the royal seaside resort of Brighton and the more elegant neighbouring town of Hove. Since the 19th century, when it became the preferred holiday destination for nobility and royalty, Brighton has developed into a liberal and artistic centre. The iconic architecture, led by the exotic Royal Pavilion, defines the cityscape just as much as the lively Brighton Palace Pier. Today, the city is known as 'London by the Sea' and attracts people from all over the world with its vibrant music scene, distinct nightlife, and its open, inclusive attitude towards minorities. The city offers a high quality of life, which is further highlighted by its location between the English Channel and the rolling hills of the South Downs."
