      "en": "Littlehampton lies on the south coast of England in West Sussex and is an important coastal town at the mouth of the River Arun. The town is primarily known as a holiday destination that offers a successful blend of traditional charm and modern leisure facilities. The harbor of Littlehampton is of great historical and economic importance and today serves as a significant marina. Visitors appreciate the long sandy beach, which attracts many vacationers, especially in the summer months. In recent years, the town has invested in the redesign of its waterfront areas to increase the quality of life for locals and visitors alike. Alongside tourism, the maritime industry also plays a role in the local economy. The geographical location offers easy access to the picturesque landscape of Sussex and nearby towns along the coast. The architecture of Littlehampton shows diversity, from Victorian villas to contemporary projects, giving the town an interesting visual identity. Littlehampton successfully combines its maritime history with the needs of modern recreation."
