      "en": "Biddulph is nestled in the hilly landscape of Staffordshire, near the border with Cheshire. The town had its origins as an agricultural community, but developed during the 19th century into a center for coal mining and the textile industry. Although these heavy industries no longer dominate today, the historical significance of mining is still palpable in the town's structure and cultural heritage. Biddulph is widely known for Biddulph Grange Garden, an impressive Victorian garden that attracts visitors from all over the country. Geographically, the town offers a good starting point for hikes and explorations in the adjacent Peak District. The local community values the preservation of the natural environment and urban well-being, maintaining a balance between modern living and the protection of cultural heritage."
