      "en": "Westbury-on-Trym is a significant suburb in the northwest of Bristol. Despite its proximity to Bristol's city center, the place has retained an independent, village-like character. The name is derived from the River Trym, which flows through the area and has significantly shaped the historical development of the place. The history of Westbury-on-Trym goes back a long way, with evidence of settlements dating back centuries, particularly around the church and monastery area. Today, it is primarily an upscale residential suburb, appreciated for its well-kept streets, good infrastructure, and historic town center. The mix of traditional architecture and more modern residential areas offers a high quality of life that makes Westbury-on-Trym one of the most desirable residential locations in Bristol, while connection to the city center is ensured by public transport."
