      "en": "Berkhamsted, situated in the picturesque valley of the River Bulbourne in Hertfordshire, is a town that impressively combines its medieval past with a modern lifestyle. The town is famous primarily for Berkhamsted Castle, a Norman motte-and-bailey castle built in the 11th century, whose impressive earthworks and walls are today a popular historic site. In the 19th century, the Grand Union Canal was built through the town, which brought economic growth and today enriches the townscape with its picturesque houseboats and towpaths. Due to the excellent train connection to London Euston, Berkhamsted has become a preferred place to live for commuters who appreciate a high quality of life in green surroundings. The combination of historical architecture, vibrant shopping opportunities, and immediate proximity to the Chiltern Hills makes Berkhamsted a unique and extremely livable place in the vicinity of London."
