      "en": "Crosland Moor is a district within the Metropolitan Borough of Kirklees in West Yorkshire. Historically, the area was heavily shaped by wool and textile production, which defined the landscape and economic structure of the region in the 19th century. Its distinctive geographical location on a hill offers panoramic views over the Colne Valley and the surrounding Pennines. Over the past decades, its character has shifted from an industrial working-class settlement to a mixed residential area. The architecture is characterized by typical Victorian terraced houses built from local sandstone. Today, the district is marked by good infrastructural links to the center of Huddersfield, while local green spaces have been maintained for the residents. The community takes pride in its cultural heritage and industrial past, which remain firmly embedded in the local identity."
