      "en": "Little Ilford is a district located within the London Borough of Newham in East London. Historically, the area was rural and part of the county of Essex, but it underwent significant urbanization during the 19th century as London rapidly expanded. Today, Little Ilford is a dense, urban environment characterized by a diverse community and a mixture of Victorian-era terraces and modern housing developments. Located near Manor Park, the area benefits from good transport links, making it a key residential suburb for those commuting into central London. While largely transformed by urban development, the district retains its own community spirit and forms an essential part of the broader social and economic fabric of the London Borough of Newham."
