      "en": "Bradford is a city in West Yorkshire that gained fame during the Industrial Revolution as the global center for wool processing. This era left behind an impressive architectural legacy, including the famous 'Little Germany' area, shaped by the wealthy German merchants of the 19th century. Today, Bradford is a culturally diverse city, known for its vibrant community and its role as a media hub. The city continuously invests in the revitalization of its town centre, transforming old industrial sites into modern cultural and commercial spaces. The economy of Bradford has shifted from manufacturing towards services, education, and tourism, making it a key economic player in the region."
