      "en": "Palmers Green is a sophisticated residential area in the London Borough of Enfield, North London. The district underwent significant development during the Edwardian era, resulting in the high-quality architecture that characterizes its main thoroughfares. It is famously known for having one of the largest Greek Cypriot populations outside of Cyprus, leading to its nickname 'Little Cyprus'. This influence is prominently visible in the local commerce, particularly along Green Lanes, which is lined with Mediterranean delis, patisseries, and tavernas. Broomfield Park is the district's primary green space, offering diverse landscapes including model boat ponds, ornamental gardens, and the shell of the historic Broomfield House. The area is also noted for its cultural associations, including being the home of poet Stevie Smith. Its combination of historic charm and multicultural vibrancy makes it a unique and desirable part of London."
