      "en": "Sketty is an affluent and highly sought-after suburb of Swansea, located on the south coast of Wales. Positioned to the west of the city centre, it rose to prominence in the 19th century as a fashionable area for the city's wealthy industrialists to build grand estates. The defining feature of Sketty is Singleton Park, a vast 250-acre public space that contains the City’s Botanical Gardens, a boating lake, and several university facilities. The district is also home to Singleton Hospital and the Singleton Park Campus of Swansea University, making it a key educational and medical hub for the region. Sketty’s architectural character is dominated by large Victorian and Edwardian terraced and detached houses, many of which have been converted into professional offices or remain as prestigious family homes. The commercial heart of the area is Sketty Cross, where the main roads meet, offering a range of local amenities, shops, and eateries. Bordering the Uplands district and lying near the gateway to the Gower Peninsula—the UK's first Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty—Sketty perfectly balances urban convenience with scenic coastal living."
