      "en": "Allestree is an affluent and verdent suburb of Derby, England, situated on the city's northern fringe. Historically a separate village mentioned in the Domesday Book of 1086, it was officially incorporated into the borough of Derby in 1968. The suburb's defining feature is Allestree Park, which covers approximately 300 acres and serves as the largest public park in the city, complete with a Grade II* listed hall and a nature reserve. Allestree also hosts the main campus of the University of Derby on Kedleston Road, lending the area a significant academic presence. The neighborhood is characterized by its prestigious housing, excellent schools, and a village-like atmosphere centered around historic buildings such as St Edmund's Church. Its location provides a scenic transition between the urban environment of Derby and the rolling hills of the Derbyshire countryside, making it one of the most desirable residential areas in the East Midlands."
