      "en": "Birkdale is a prestigious residential area and suburb of Southport in the county of Merseyside, Northwest England. It is most famous for its association with world-class golf; the Royal Birkdale Golf Club is a staple of the Open Championship rotation and is consistently ranked among the finest links courses globally. The aesthetic of Birkdale is defined by wide, tree-lined avenues and large Victorian and Edwardian houses that speak to the area's growth during the 19th-century boom of coastal resorts. Birkdale Village serves as the local commercial hub, retaining a distinctive 'village' feel with a variety of independent shops, wine bars, and upscale eateries. Geographically, the area is separated from the Irish Sea by a massive system of sand dunes, which are of significant ecological importance and provide a unique backdrop for the coastal properties. The arrival of the railway in the 1840s transformed Birkdale from a quiet hamlet into a sought-after retreat for the wealthy merchants of Liverpool."
