      "en": "Bradwell is a large village and civil parish in Norfolk, England, situated just to the south-west of the seaside resort of Great Yarmouth. Historically, the area is significant for its proximity to the Roman fort of Burgh Castle, which served as a vital coastal defense during the 3rd century. In the modern era, Bradwell has transitioned into a thriving residential hub, absorbing much of the population growth from the surrounding coastal districts. The village boasts several schools, community centers, and shopping areas, while maintaining easy access to the scenic Norfolk Broads. Its strategic location makes it a gateway for tourists heading to the Norfolk coast, and its local economy is supported by a mix of retail, services, and small-scale industries that cater to the Broads' agricultural and tourism sectors. The parish has expanded considerably since the mid-20th century, becoming one of the most populous villages in the county while retaining its distinct identity."
