      "en": "Sharoe Green is a prominent residential district located in the northern suburbs of Preston, Lancashire, within the parish of Fulwood. The area is most notably defined by the presence of the Royal Preston Hospital, a major teaching hospital and tertiary center that serves as a cornerstone of the regional healthcare infrastructure. This institutional presence has shaped the district into a hub for medical professionals and associated services. Beyond its medical significance, Sharoe Green is characterized by its affluent suburban atmosphere, featuring a mix of mid-20th-century housing, spacious detached properties, and leafy residential streets. The district benefits from excellent educational facilities, including several highly-rated primary and secondary schools. Its strategic location offers easy access to the Preston city center via main arterial roads, as well as proximity to the M6 motorway junction at Broughton. With various local amenities, green spaces, and a reputedly high quality of life, Sharoe Green remains one of the most sought-after residential locations in the Preston metropolitan area, balancing urban convenience with a quiet, community-focused environment."
