      "en": "High Park is a prominent residential area located on the eastern fringe of Southport, within the Metropolitan Borough of Sefton, Merseyside. Established during the late Victorian and Edwardian periods, the district grew rapidly as Southport transformed into a premier coastal resort. The area is characterized by a mix of traditional terraced housing and semi-detached suburban homes, reflecting its evolution over the last century. High Park serves as a vital community hub with its own distinct identity, centered around the local amenities of Bispham Road and the nearby Meols Cop retail and industrial zones. A key transportation asset for the district is the Meols Cop railway station, which provides regular services to Liverpool and Manchester, making it an ideal location for commuters. While situated inland from the main Southport seafront, residents enjoy easy access to the town's parks and coastal attractions. The district is home to a diverse population of approximately 8,000 people and is known for its strong local schools and community organizations. Recent years have seen ongoing investment in local infrastructure, ensuring that High Park remains an attractive and accessible part of the wider Merseyside metropolitan area."
