      "en": "Oxhey is a prestigious and green suburb located in the southern part of Watford, Hertfordshire. Its name suggests ancient origins as a clearing for oxen, but the area's modern character was forged during the Victorian era with the arrival of the London and Birmingham Railway. A standout historical site is the Oxhey Chapel, built in 1612 on the site of a medieval manor, representing a rare example of a private chapel from the Jacobean period. Geographically, Oxhey is defined by its abundance of mature trees and open spaces, with Oxhey Park serving as a major recreational hub along the River Colne. The suburb is known for its strong sense of community and distinctive 'Oxhey Village' area, which features traditional brick-built cottages. With its excellent schools and fast rail connections to London Euston via Bushey station, it remains one of the most desirable residential areas in the region."
