      "en": "Abersychan is a historic town located in the Torfaen valley of South Wales, near the town of Pontypool. Its rise to prominence began in the early 19th century during the Industrial Revolution, when it became a powerhouse of iron production and coal mining. The establishment of the Abersychan Ironworks in 1826 catalyzed the town's growth, leading to the construction of vast rows of terraced housing for the growing workforce. At its peak, the town was a bustling urban center with numerous shops, schools, and cultural institutions reflecting the prosperity of the Victorian era. However, the 20th century brought challenges as heavy industry declined, eventually leading to the closure of the mines and factories. In recent years, Abersychan has focused on heritage conservation and environmental restoration. The town is part of the Gwent Valleys and serves as a gateway to the nearby Blaenavon World Heritage site, offering a glimpse into the industrial past while embracing a quieter, community-focused future."
